Agentic Automation Platform for SMBs

1. Project Overview
Vision & Purpose
The goal of this project is to create an automated platform for small and medium businesses (SMBs) that handles operational and marketing tasks. The system leverages an Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework with multiple Master Control Programs (MCPs) orchestrated by a central conductor. This enables tasks like email management, website content generation, and social media management to run smoothly with human oversight.

Key Objectives
Automate Repetitive Tasks: Streamline operational tasks (e.g., managing emails, generating content) to reduce manual work.

Improve Accuracy and Efficiency: Use specialized agents (MCPs) to ensure accurate data retrieval and task execution.

Provide Human Oversight: Integrate a dashboard for monitoring, approvals, and feedback.

Scalable and Modular: Design the system so that additional modules (e.g., ticket booking, inventory management) can be added as needed.

2. High-Level Vision Deck (One-Pager)
Concept Overview
Central Conductor MCP: Acts as the brain that routes requests to specialized modules.

Specialized MCP Modules:

Email MCP: Automatically handles incoming emails, replies, and customer inquiries.

Content Generation MCP: Creates, optimizes, and schedules website and blog content.

Additional Modules: Potential for scheduling, booking, and other operational tasks.

Benefits
Operational Efficiency: Automation of routine tasks frees up business owners to focus on strategy.

Data-Driven Decisions: Real-time data integration (weather, analytics, etc.) enhances service quality.

Scalability: A modular design means the platform can grow with the business.

Human in the Loop: The dashboard allows for approvals and adjustments, ensuring quality and control.

