3. Technical Architecture Details
Core Components
Conductor MCP:

Role: Acts as the central orchestrator. Receives tasks, analyzes context, and assigns them to the relevant specialized MCP.

Responsibilities: Task routing, error handling, combining outputs from various MCPs, and ensuring a cohesive workflow.

Email MCP:

Role: Connects to email servers and handles incoming/outgoing communication.

Responsibilities: Auto-reply generation, spam filtering, and flagging emails for human approval via the dashboard.

Content Generation MCP:

Role: Creates and optimizes content for websites, blogs, and social media.

Responsibilities: Pulling SEO data, generating text and images, scheduling posts, and sending for human approval.

Additional Modules (e.g., Scheduling/Booking MCPs):

Role: Manage domain-specific tasks such as appointment scheduling, booking management, etc.

Responsibilities: Integrate with external APIs (e.g., booking platforms) and manage real-time data.

Integration & Communication
API-Driven: All MCPs communicate via standardized APIs, ensuring modularity and easy integration.

Event-Driven Workflow: The conductor triggers specific MCPs based on events (e.g., an incoming email or a scheduled content post).

Human Oversight Layer: The dashboard provides notifications, visual reports, and approval controls for each action.

